The quintessential companion to enchiladas, tacos, and carnitas. Rather than gummy or scorched rice, this Instant Pot method toasts long-grain white rice in fragrant oil with onions and garlic before pressure cooking in seasoned chicken broth and tomato sauce for perfectly separated, tender, flavorful grains.

*Adapted from [Allrecipes](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/263330/instant-pot-mexican-rice/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 tablespoon avocado oil or neutral vegetable oil
- ½ medium yellow onion, finely chopped
- 2 large cloves garlic, finely minced
- 1 cup long-grain white rice (rinsed in a fine mesh sieve until water runs clear, then drained)
- 1 ¾ cups low-sodium chicken stock or broth
- ½ cup plain tomato sauce (canned)
- 1 teaspoon kosher salt
- ¼ teaspoon ground cumin
- 1 pinch cayenne pepper
- Fresh cilantro, chopped (for serving)
- Fresh lime wedges

## Instructions

1. **Rinse the Rice First:** Place 1 cup of long-grain white rice in a fine-mesh strainer and rinse under cold water for 60 seconds until the runoff turns clear. Shake off excess water. Rinsing strips excess surface starch, preventing gummy, clumpy rice.
2. **Sauté the Onions and Garlic:** Set the Instant Pot to **Sauté** (Medium/Normal). Pour in the avocado oil. Add the chopped onion and cook, stirring occasionally, for 4 to 5 minutes until soft and translucent. Stir in the minced garlic and sauté for 30 seconds until fragrant.
3. **Toast the Grains:** Dump the drained rice directly into the hot pot. Stir constantly for 2 to 3 minutes to coat every grain in oil and lightly toast them until they turn opaque with a light golden hue and nutty aroma.
4. **Deglaze Thoroughly:** Pour in the chicken stock. Immediately use a flat wooden spatula to firmly scrape the entire bottom surface of the inner pot. Releasing any toasted starches or garlic stuck to the bottom is essential to prevent the cooker's "Burn" notice.
5. **Add Tomato and Seasonings:** Pour in the ½ cup of tomato sauce, kosher salt, ground cumin, and cayenne pepper. Stir once to distribute evenly. Press **Cancel** to turn off Sauté mode.
6. **Pressure Cook on High:** Lock the lid onto the Instant Pot and set the steam release valve to **Sealing**. Select **Manual / Pressure Cook** on **HIGH** and set the timer for **9 minutes**.
7. **Short Rest & Vent:** When cooking completes, allow the pot to sit undisturbed for **5 minutes** of natural release. Then carefully turn the steam valve to **Venting** to discharge any remaining steam. Unlock the lid.
8. **Rest, Fluff, and Serve:** Let the uncovered rice sit in the pot for 2 minutes to let surface moisture evaporate, then gently fluff and fold with a fork. Spoon into bowls, garnish with freshly chopped cilantro, and serve with fresh lime wedges.

## Notes

- **Tomato Paste Swap:** In place of ½ cup tomato sauce, you can whisk 2 tablespoons of tomato paste into the warm chicken broth before adding.
- **Vegetable Add-ins:** Toss in ½ cup of frozen sweet corn or rinsed black beans right before locking the lid.
